# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# wrapround.part -- A cylinder face that reaches round its axis past the seam
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# The union leaves face s13.c12.0 on all but 13 degrees of its cylinder,
# and its loop runs across the angle opposite the middle of the face.
# The mesh took the angle of each point by that middle, so one edge
# jumped a full turn and the lines of the face did not pair (fuzzer
# finding 0033); it now runs the angles on round each loop.
circle c1 12.5 6 29.5 along z
extrude s2 from 15 to 0 c1
circle c3 0.5 13.5 -4.5 along x
extrude s4 from 13 to 13.2546 c3 draft 41
common s5 s2 s4
profile p6 along z -6 5.5 0 28.5 5.5 0 28.5 2.5 0 -6 2.5 0.5
extrude s7 from 15.5 to 2 p6
union s8 s5 s7
profile p9 along x -15 7 0.5 20.5 -5 2 -15 -5 1.5
extrude s10 from 3 to 30 p9
union s11 s8 s10
circle c12 12 5.5 -1 along x
extrude s13 from 2 to 15.5 c12
union s14 s11 s13
